# Behind its first yield a generator asks how it was resumed: to throw, to return, or to go on. The mode is an integer from 0 to 2 in a register. The walk boxed it and compared it twice with boxed constants by the generic form:
# two entries of the stub Equal.StrictInFlags at the first step of every generator (TypeScript 6: 650,936 in one function).
# f1 = count
# RUN: walk f1:CoroutineBody mechanisms=all
# CHECK: int[0, 2] @Int32 = ResultAt {{*}} index=1
# CHECK-NOT: = Box
# CHECK: boolean @Boolean = StrictEq {{*}} form=Integers
# CHECK-NOT: = Box
# CHECK: boolean @Boolean = StrictEq {{*}} form=Integers
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWERS: 012 left true true thrown true
# ANSWERS-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(NONE): run-in-shell mechanisms=none
# NONE: 012 left true true thrown true
# NONE-NEXT: exited with 0
